      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's a good start, i like the focus on the schools and the park. it feels grounded. but i just ran it through the tool and the \"inspiration metric\" came back way too low. like, really low. the analytics team is worried it's gonna feel a bit too \"subdued\" or dry for a big rally crowd. \n\ncan we punch it up? i don't want it to be ridiculous, but we definitely need more of that emotional, descriptive language to get that score up into a better range. maybe focus on the \"shared spirit\" or the \"strength\" of the community to help drive those numbers up without losing the point? just try to make it feel more... vibrant?",
      "source": "evaluator"
